# D-108: a call inside the actual of a Structure-typed formal is checked as any actual is.  `mk` stores an
# int into a size_t field -- a conversion, whose failure is the implicit throw `convert` -- so it is a
# throwing method; `go` calls it only inside `rd(mk(5))`.  The check took the admission path for that
# actual and never looked into it: no edge go -> mk, the throw closure left `go` non-throwing, and the
# L1 called mk with a status `go` did not have (gcc: 'l2_msg' / 'l2_out_throw' undeclared).  An implicit
# throw needs no catch (Q11): `go` becomes throwing, the root is its caller.  5 through the field; success
# is 7.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
end: Model
fn: mk (int: v) Model
    x: merge Model
    x\a: v
    return: x
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
fn: go () size_t
return: rd(mk(5))

size_t: got 0U
got: go()
int: ok 1
if: got = 5U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
